            "target_entity_instance": "tropical regions",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "The comparison between the SOI and the calculated monthly global isoprene emissions anomalies (Fig. 5) indicates a negative correlation. The correlation coefficient (r) between the SOI and monthly global biogenic emissions anomalies, calculated for the period 1983\u20131995, is -0.28 for isoprene, -0.14 for monoterpenes and -0.01 for methanol. These values are in qualitative agreement with Naik et al. (2004) but of smaller absolute correlation (-0.54 for isoprene and -0.24 for monoterpenes for 1971\u20131990, in Naik et al., 2004). The correlation coefficients obtained are rather small but it is however interesting to note that the correlation between biogenic emissions and SOI is somewhat higher in tropical regions compared to other regions, as shown in Fig. 6 for isoprene.",
